    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d177">

                <pb facs="0367" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5758/4</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Magruder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July 23,
                        1925</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 13.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 529</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    instruction No. 123 of April 21, 1925, (no File No.), respecting the appointment
                    of Customs Attachés, and to the Legation’s reply thereto No. 479 of May 25,
                        1925.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d177-f1"/> I have the honor to report that I am
                    now in receipt of a note <pb facs="0368" n="242" xml:id="pg242"/> from the
                    Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs, a copy and translation of which are
                    herewith enclosed, to the effect that the Swedish Government regrets that it is
                    not in a position to give a favorable reply to the request that customs attachés
                    be recognized as members of the Legation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alexander R.
                    Magruder</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d177-a1.xml" xpointer="d177-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
